---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const p='/equipment/03-08/',photo='https://scscoatings.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/2010_labcoater2.pdf',manual='https://bionium.miami.edu/_assets/pdf/manuals/from-vendors-3/scs-coter.pdf';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Labcoter 2 dry geometry witness" subtitle="" wide={true} description="Inspect pre-authored geometry tags on an inert witness coupon inside a visual Labcoter 2 reference."><script is:inline>window.scsWitness=import('/equipment/03-08/witness.mjs');</script><article class="equipment" id="scswitness"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/03-08/">← Equipment 03-08</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#scs-ref">References</a><a href="#scs-proof">Verification</a></nav><header class="eq-mast"><p class="eq-meta">03-08 / READ-ONLY GEOMETRIC WITNESS</p><h2>Inspect the faces. Keep P1 open.</h2><p class="eq-lede">Inspect fixed before-and-after tags on a small inert coupon. The top and right wall each show a 2.5 µm normal offset, while the protected contact stays at zero. Nothing is deposited or changed by this viewer.</p></header>
<div class="cols"><section><p class="eq-meta">01 / REFERENCE MODEL</p><h3>SCS PDS 2010 Labcoter 2</h3><div id="scs-view" aria-label="Metric exterior of Labcoter 2 with dry witness holder"></div><small id="scs-model" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</small><div class="tools"><button id="scs-whole">Whole instrument</button><button id="scs-bay">Dry holder</button><button id="scs-coupon">Coupon close-up</button><button id="scs-cut">Show display-only cutaway</button></div><p>The cabinet and chamber are a scale reference. Hide the illustrated sleeve to see an authored dry witness on its platform. This is not a model of a mechanical lid, functional internals or hardware controls.</p></section>
<section><p class="eq-meta">02 / READ-ONLY INSPECTION</p><h3>Select fixed coordinate tags</h3><label>Synthetic fixture<select id="scs-fixture"><option value="masked">Matched geometric witness</option><option value="contact-mark">Pre-authored P1 offset fault</option></select></label><label>Face focus<select id="scs-face"><option value="TOP-EXPOSED">TOP · exposed face</option><option value="SIDE-EXPOSED">SIDE · right wall</option><option value="P1">P1 · protected contact</option></select></label><div class="tools"><button id="scs-scan" class="run">Inspect tags</button><button id="scs-reset">Reset witness</button></div><p id="scs-status" role="status">Fixed geometric reference loaded.</p><canvas id="scs-diagram" width="620" height="238" aria-label="Magnified local-normal schematic, offsets not to scale"></canvas></section></div>
<section><p class="eq-meta">03 / FACE GEOMETRY</p><h3>Offsets and mask state</h3><p id="scs-result" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="over"><table><thead><tr><th>Face ID</th><th>Mask</th><th>Expected µm</th><th>Actual µm</th><th>Check</th></tr></thead><tbody id="scs-rows"></tbody></table></div><div class="tools"><button id="scs-save" disabled>Export inspection JSON</button><a href={p+'example-witness.json'}>Example inspected witness</a></div></section>
<section id="scs-ref"><p class="eq-meta">04 / EXTERIOR REFERENCE</p><h3>Original reconstruction, one documented configuration</h3><p>The <a href={photo+'#page=1'}>Specialty Coating Systems Labcoter 2 brochure photo</a> establishes the narrow cabinet, front control strip, cylindrical hood and viewing window. The <a href={manual}>SCS PDS 2010 Operator’s Manual Rev 48, §2.1 dimensional table</a> gives nominal cabinet width, depth and height of 495 × 604 × 1283 mm and a nominal 12 × 12 in (304.8 mm) chamber. The model uses nominal exterior envelope; local hardware, rear jacket, holder, wall details and case edges are inferred. No measurement or vendor drawing is republished. This is Labcoter 2, not the later Labcoter 3 option.</p><div class="tools"><a href={p+'build-model.py'} download>Editable Blender source</a><a href={p+'labcoter2.glb'} download>Download GLB</a><a href={p+'xr.json'}>Named VR targets and dimensions</a><a href={p+'witness.mjs'}>Inspection state and geometry code</a></div></section>
<section id="scs-proof"><p class="eq-meta">05 / VERIFICATION AND LIMITS</p><h3>A geometric check, not a coating run</h3><p>The displayed offset is Δr·n from the two fixed coordinates and a declared unit normal. Tangential error is the length of Δr−(Δr·n)n. The protected tag P1 expects 0 µm normally and tangentially. The faulty fixture includes a pre-authored 0.5 µm offset at P1 so a numerical mismatch can be detected. The value is not a physical prediction.</p><p><b>Verified:</b> both exposed tags exactly 2.5 µm, protected P1 exactly zero; the alternate fixture flags only P1 with 0.5 µm offset (1×10⁻⁶ µm mathematical tolerance, not instrument accuracy). Seven GLB geometry checks accompany the downloadable model. The <code>bts.dry-witness-report.v1</code> output preserves witness, face and contact IDs, input points, frame, units and reporting revision. No geometry is generated by a process, and there is no recipe, mass-gain model, operating setting, heating, vacuum, exposure, materials or physical hardware control. No headset validation is claimed.</p></section>
</article></Layout><script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/03-08/client.mjs';</script><style is:global>
#scswitness .cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.13fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:.8rem}#scswitness section{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:1rem;margin:.8rem 0;min-width:0}#scswitness .cols section{margin:0}#scswitness .eq-meta{margin:0}#scswitness h3{margin:.3rem 0 .61rem;font-size:1.5rem}#scswitness .tools{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:.43rem;margin:.65rem 0}#scswitness label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;margin:.55rem 0}#scswitness button,#scswitness select{min-height:40px;padding:.37rem;max-width:100%;font:inherit;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--panel,transparent);color:var(--text)}#scswitness button{cursor:pointer}#scswitness button.run{background:#365f57;color:white}#scswitness button:disabled{opacity:.5}#scs-view{height:clamp(270px,32vw,410px);background:#273337}#scs-view canvas{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;touch-action:none}#scs-diagram{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}#scswitness .over{overflow:auto}#scswitness table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}#scswitness th,#scswitness td{text-align:left;padding:.43rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}#scs-result{font-weight:bold}#scswitness code{overflow-wrap:anywhere}@media(max-width:760px){#scswitness .cols{grid-template-columns:1fr}#scswitness section{padding:.68rem}}
</style>
